    "product_id": "dfbf6d2e-62f2-4bf5-8af2-5942549b2250",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 300815\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n115 AM PDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Mild weather and warming temperatures are expected through the \n  weekend into early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Tuesday.\n\nRidging will build over the region as the trough responsible for \nMonday and Tuesday's storms moves into New Mexico today. Rising \n500 mb heights will allow for temperatures across the area to \nrebound, with warmer than normal temperatures returning by \nThursday. In addition to warmer than normal temperatures, lighter \nwinds and dry conditions will also accompany this ridge. Weather \nwill remain warm and mild through the weekend. Long term guidance \nshows a shortwave trough approaching the West Coast as we head \ninto next week, which will result in southerly breezes and \nincreased cloud cover. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package... \nNorth winds will continue to diminish late this evening becoming \nlight and variable overnight. Hi-re guidance continues to indicate \nstronger NW drainage winds developing around and after 13z, \ntherefore keeping NW (320) winds around 10-15 kt gusting over 20 kt \noccasionally 13z through around 18z when winds should still remain \nNW-NNW but diminish under 10 kts. Winds then go light and variable \nafter sunset tomorrow night. Ceilings will improve overnight \ntonight remaining VFR aoa 10kft, clearing by mid-morning. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package... Radar shows showers \ncontinuing to diminish around the CRV this evening. Keeping VCSH in \nthe TAF for KEED and KIFP through 09z then dry conditions thereafter. \nAll other sites should remain dry as clouds slowly clear through the \novernight hours. Gusty northerly winds will taper off through the \nevening, becoming lighter overnight for most and with lingering \nnortherly flow on Wednesday. The main exception will be KDAG/the \nwestern Mojave, where winds return to the west overnight through the \nend of the forecast period. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Moore\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
